# eza — real-world examples

## List all files including hidden

```sh
eza --all
```

## Tree view, three levels deep

```sh
eza --long --tree --level=3
```

## Long listing with headers, icons, and git status

```sh
eza --long --header --icons --git
```

## Newest files last — see what changed recently in a log dir

```sh
eza -l --sort=modified /var/log
```

## Directories only, e.g. survey the media library layout

```sh
eza -lD /srv/plex
```

## Human sizes plus group column, checking ownership on a share

```sh
eza -lag /home/david/Public
```

## Recurse into subdirectories without tree lines

```sh
eza -lR ~/scripts
```

| Flag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| -l, --long | detailed listing |
| -a, --all | include hidden files |
| -T, --tree | tree view (with --level=N depth) |
| -D, --only-dirs | list directories only |
| -R, --recurse | recurse into directories |
| --git | show git status per file |
| --icons | file-type icons |
| --sort=FIELD | name, size, modified, extension |

```sh
eza --help
```
